# /etc/cron.d/fxmily-worker — Fxmily AI worker schedule on the server (J9).
#
# Owner   : root (system crond reads /etc/cron.d/* with mode 0644).
# User    : fxmily (each row's 6th field — non-privileged execution).
# Wrapper : /usr/local/bin/fxmily-worker (ops/cron/fxmily-worker) — it holds the
#           PATH/HOME/allowlist/log/timeout/heartbeat plumbing; all the WORKER
#           semantics (global lock, jittered sleeps, quota cooldown, `claude auth
#           status` pre-flight, status.json, exit-75 remap) stay in
#           ops/worker/run-batch.sh, ported from Windows unchanged.
#
# ⚠ TIMEZONE — this host runs Europe/Paris (/etc/localtime) and Debian vixie-cron
# interprets /etc/cron.d hour fields in the HOST-LOCAL timezone (no CRON_TZ).
# Proven at runtime on this box for /etc/cron.d/fxmily-app (see its header). The
# hours below are therefore PARIS WALL-CLOCK and reproduce the Windows Task
# Scheduler times 1:1 — which is what J9 requires ("reproduire les schedules en
# heure Paris") and what is DST-proof for a French cohort.
#
# ⚠ SEPARATE FILE, on purpose. The 25 app-side rows live in /etc/cron.d/fxmily-app
# and are converged by the root `fxmily-sync-cron` validator. Keeping the worker
# in its OWN file means (a) a worker rollback is `rm /etc/cron.d/fxmily-worker`
# with zero risk of touching an app cron, and (b) the app validator's line-shape
# regex is never asked to accept a new command name.
#
# ── Schedule (mirrors ops/worker/install-worker.ps1 $Pipelines) ──────────────
#
#   onboarding    every 20 min at :01/:21/:41   — the pipeline that kills the
#                                                 "IA silence 24h après profil"
#   verification  every 5 min  at :03..:58      — MT5 proofs analysed while the
#                                                 member is still waiting; an
#                                                 empty pull short-circuits
#                                                 before any claude call
#   seances       every 30 min 08h-23h          — J9 scope 5: the séances
#                                                 pipeline joins the worker
#                                                 contract (lock/status/log/
#                                                 heartbeat). Reconcile+report
#                                                 only; see the script header
#                                                 for why its AI leg is
#                                                 operator-side by design
#   calendar      daily  05h10
#   weekly        Sunday 05h40
#   monthly       day 1  06h10
#   profile       day 2  06h40                  — one day after the debrief
#   watchdog      every 30 min at :07/:37       — verifies this very file + the
#                                                 claude auth, then POSTs the
#                                                 heartbeat /admin/system reads
#
# Minutes are staggered so two pipelines never start on the same tick. A
# collision is harmless anyway (the loser skips cleanly on the global lock and
# the next tick picks the work up, idempotently) — the stagger just keeps the
# logs readable.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
MAILTO=""

1,21,41 * * * *              fxmily   /usr/local/bin/fxmily-worker onboarding
3-58/5 * * * *               fxmily   /usr/local/bin/fxmily-worker verification
25,55 8-23 * * *             fxmily   /usr/local/bin/fxmily-worker seances
10 5 * * *                   fxmily   /usr/local/bin/fxmily-worker calendar
40 5 * * 0                   fxmily   /usr/local/bin/fxmily-worker weekly
10 6 1 * *                   fxmily   /usr/local/bin/fxmily-worker monthly
40 6 2 * *                   fxmily   /usr/local/bin/fxmily-worker profile
7,37 * * * *                 fxmily   /usr/local/bin/fxmily-worker-watchdog
